-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Solomon's Key
  Publisher   U.S. Gold, 1987
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Solomon's Key (1987)(U.S. Gold).z80
  MD5         23ee5b2123dbc8a9a5daccbd51db4db0

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    The Spec256 conversion's colours on every figure: Dana, the
              goblins, dragons, flames and fireballs in their own colours over
              the unchanged rooms. No white outlines or edges. Source:
              Enhanced colours: from the Spec256 conversion (the Spectrum
              Magic package, credited to Spec256), painter not established.

  Pace        original (+0.12% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless; probe 37799
              (the main loop, once a pass); input keyed to passes; lockstep on
              the pass and bonus counters; 10 trials per scene of 400 passes
              (level 10: 5, a fixture started there))

  Changes     1.0: figures as Next sprites; the hooks in Sinclair's 48K ROM as
              the whole alt ROM; the game's speed restored after every hook; R
              kept as the original's; the original's pace kept from the game's
              own pass padding; the tape's loading screen; the Spec256
              conversion's colours as the Enhanced set

  Note        Keys: a key on the loading screen, then hold 1 on the title
              until the room builds (the tune reads its keys between notes).
              In play O left, P right, Q jump, A crouch, SPACE makes or breaks
              a block, V throws a fireball. Every moving figure is a Next
              sprite, bright white with a black body, the look the owner
              approved; the rooms, blocks and panel keep the original's
              colours. The game plays at the original's pace: the hooks' time
              is repaid from the game's own padding of each pass; passes with
              ten figures or more have none, and repay it in the next padded
              passes. All four of the archive's cheats are on the menu, each
              shown to work in the simulator. Not tested on hardware.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Infinite fireballs
   3  Immunity
   4  Infinite time

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

