-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      Played by the owner in JNext 2026-11-05: approved

  Replay      IDENTICAL on 6 recordings, 202,364 frames, every hook run
              (362,151 plots, 54,874 commits, 144 clears, 206,127 pads): at
              every hook original and patched code compared from the same
              state, every register with R, memory, the screen bit for bit
              (sprites over the patched screen = the original's), and each
              hook's debt change against its modelled time over the
              original's; 12 of 12 negatives detected, a forced 3.5 MHz exit
              (replayed at 7 MHz) among them; ROM path check clean on both
              builds, apart from the reads the record accepts: the game's
              delay copies ROM onto itself, and with 16,384 bytes (sk_o1)
              reads the hook bytes, which nothing uses; the Enhanced build
              differs from the default only in its patterns and 16 palette
              bytes, none of them read by a hook

  Emulator    JNext 1.1.104 headless: the tape's loading screen, the title and
              play reached from the .nxc's menu builds in both colour sets,
              cheats on and off, frames inspected; flicker check clean in both
              sets (300 frames); 15-minute soak in both sets: no freeze, loop
              or crash, play, game overs and restarts on the sheet

  Coverage    Random-walk recordings only, no human play: rooms 0-16 and the
              secret room 20 with cheats, deaths by enemies and the timer,
              game over, high score, title, restart; the level end by a poke;
              not reached: a room solved by play, 4 plot callers (enemy
              states)

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
